 "final_text": "**Reply to Robin:**\n\nFound it in this morning's bank file (`bank-file-2026-03-01.xlsx`, row 3):\n\n> ACH RETURN \u2013 LAMNA HEALTHCARE \u2013 ORIGINAL 2026-02-24 \u2014 **-$18,000.00**, reason **R01 insufficient funds** (plus a separate $25 return fee on our side)\n\n**What it undoes:** ACH receipt **LHPAY-77** ($18,000.00), which Lamna sent 2026-02-24 and which the ERP applied in full against invoice **LHINV-001** (\"January platform fees,\" $18,000, due 2026-02-14). That invoice is still showing **closed** in the ERP \u2014 it hasn't caught up with the return yet \u2014 so it needs to be reopened.\n\n**What Lamna actually owes right now**, combining the ERP's other open items with the reopened invoice:\n- LHINV-002 (January usage overage) \u2014 open, $9,500.00\n- LHINV-003 (February platform fees) \u2014 open, $7,700.00\n- LHINV-001 (reopened due to the bounced payment) \u2014 $18,000.00\n\n**True open balance: $35,200.00** (vs. $17,200.00 currently shown in the ERP).\n\nRecommend flagging the account and reopening LHINV-001 in the system before any further collections outreach relies on the stale balance.",
